{title: From Mesha Toward Sephar}
{subtitle: Genesis 10:27; 10:28–30; 1 Chronicles 1:21; Genesis 10:21–26; Ezekiel 27:19}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Sons of Shem [Dm7]rose after the flood
[Eb]Elam and Asshur stood in the wood
[Bb]Arpachshad led [Dm7]his children along
[Eb]Shelah and Eber carried the song
[Bb]Eber had two [Dm7]sons in that day
[Eb]Peleg when earth was divided away
[Bb]His brother Joktan [Dm7]took the east
[Eb]Settling the lands from north to the least
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
From Me[Bb]sha toward Sephar we [Dm7]go
Hill country of the [Eb]east, steady and slow
Hadoram and [Bb]Uzal walk be[Dm7]side
Diklah and O[Eb]bal sharing the tide
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Abimael and She[Dm7]ba follow in line
[Eb]Ophir and Havilah crossed the design
[Bb]Jobab stands firm with [Dm7]the sons of the land
[Eb]Thirteen names written across the land
[Bb]All these were the [Dm7]sons of Joktan
[Eb]Settled in the eastern mountain plain
[Bb]Chronicled again [Dm7]in the scroll
[Eb]Confirming the line as faithful and whole
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
From Me[Bb]sha toward Sephar we [Dm7]go
Hill country of the [Eb]east, steady and slow
Hadoram and U[Bb]zal walk be[Dm7]side
Diklah and O[Eb]bal sharing the tide
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Ezekiel speaks of the [Dm7]trade of Tyre
[Eb]Vedan and Javan from Uzal by
[Bb]Wrought iron and cassia in [Dm7]hand
[Eb]Cane in the market, a foreign land
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From Me[Bb]sha toward Sephar we [Dm7]go
Hill country of the east, [Eb]steady and slow
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×3
| [Bb] |
